    "slug": "puntland-forces-take-control-of-third-federal-military-base-in-bari-region",
    "summary": "Puntland security forces seized a federal military base in Carmo, Bari region, marking the third such takeover this month. The move is part of a broader effort to consolidate control over security within Puntland, raising tensions with the federal government.",
    "content": "On Saturday, Puntland regional security forces took control of a military base belonging to the Somali federal government in the town of Carmo, located in the Bari region, approximately 100 kilometers from the port city of Bosaso. The operation occurred without any reported clashes, according to a statement from regional police, who said the base was dismantled as part of a broader campaign to bring all armed forces under Puntland's authority.\n\nThis seizure marks the third such action this month, following similar takeovers of federal bases in other parts of Puntland. The move is part of a wider effort by Puntland authorities to strip Mogadishu-aligned troops from the region and ensure that the use of force rests exclusively with the regional administration. This comes amid ongoing disputes between Puntland and the federal government over control of security and resources, which have simmered for years.\n\nThe federal government has not yet issued an official response to the latest development, but previous takeovers have drawn criticism from Mogadishu, which views such actions as undermining the country's unity and constitutional order. Puntland, however, has long argued that it needs greater autonomy to manage its own security, especially given the challenges posed by piracy and militant groups in the region.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, these events highlight the continuing fragility of central authority and the persistent regional dynamics that shape daily life in Somalia. Many in the diaspora closely monitor such developments as they consider investments or travel back to their homeland, and the control of security forces often impacts perceptions of stability. The situation remains fluid, and observers expect further discussions between Puntland and federal authorities over the distribution of power.\n\nRead the original report from Somalia Guardian here: https://www.somaliguardian.com/news/somalia-news/somalia-puntland-seizes-third-federal-base-carmo-bari/",
    "source": "somaliguardian.com",
    "source_name": "Somalia Guardian",
