    "content": "Mogadishu, Somalia — The Puntland regional administration has officially assumed command of federal military units based in the town of Carmo, according to a statement released today. The transfer of authority, which took effect immediately, places the day-to-day operational control of these forces under Puntland's security leadership.\n\nCarmo, located in the Bari region, has been a focal point for security operations in recent years due to its proximity to areas where militant groups have been active. The handover is part of broader efforts to harmonize command structures between the federal government and regional administrations, which have often operated with overlapping mandates.\n\nPuntland officials said the move aims to streamline decision-making and enhance rapid response capabilities in the area. The federal Ministry of Defense confirmed the transition, noting that it follows a series of technical consultations between the two parties. No further details were provided regarding the specific number of troops affected or any changes to their deployment.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this development signals a step toward more coherent security governance in a region that has historically experienced tensions between Mogadishu and Garowe. It also underscores the growing role of regional administrations in managing local security, a trend that diaspora communities often monitor closely due to its implications for stability and investment.\n\nThe takeover has so far proceeded peacefully, with no reported incidents. Observers expect that Puntland will now integrate these forces into its broader operational framework, potentially affecting future counter-militancy efforts in the area.\n\nRead the original report from Horseed Media here: https://horseedmedia.net/puntland-oo-la-wareegtey-taliskii-ciidamada-heer-federal-ee-degmada-carmo/424593/",
